rgbjs's own code (src/, rust/*/src, scripts/, test/*.js) is MIT licensed; see LICENSE.

The WebAssembly files in wasm/ are compiled from third-party crates, mainly
Apache-2.0 licensed, including:

  wasm/v011: rgb-invoicing, rgb-ops, rgb-consensus, rgb-schemas, rgb-aluvm,
             rgb-strict-encoding, rgb-strict-types (0.11.1 / 1.0.x)
             https://github.com/rgb-protocol
  wasm/v012: rgb-std, rgb-invoice, rgb-runtime, rgb-psbt and rgb-descriptors
             0.12.0-rc.3, sonic-callreq, sonic-api, hypersonic, ultrasonic,
             bp-core, bp-std, bp-derive, psbt, strict_types
             (RGB-WG / AluVM / LNP-BP); chrono and indexmap (MIT or Apache-2.0). rust/v012/src/mem.rs is ported from
             sonic-persist-fs 0.12.0 and rgb-persist-fs 0.12.0-rc.3.
             https://github.com/RGB-WG https://github.com/AluVM

Exact versions and the full dependency list are in rust/v011/Cargo.lock and
rust/v012/Cargo.lock. Each crate's license applies to its compiled code.

rust/patches/strict_encoding-2.9.1 and rust/patches/strict_types-2.9.1 are LNP/BP's
crates (Apache-2.0) with one change each, described in their RGBJS-PATCH.md;
wasm/v012 is built with them.

rust/v012/issuers/RGB20-FNA.issuer is copied from RGB-WG/rgb v0.12.0-rc.3
examples/; the RGB21 and RGB25 issuers from pandora-prime/rgb-issuers at
49b4048 (all Apache-2.0). They are compiled into wasm/v012 as trusted issuers.

Test vectors in test/vectors/ that come from upstream tests or fixtures say
where they come from in the README next to them.
